zc6 = z3x + GRAB_MICRO_L (GrabMicro.java, an existing switch never on z3x, now under the ledger with a budget test: switch bot bots/zgl = zl0 + three ledgered hooks + two Cfg lines; bundle.sh zc6 zl0 z3x zgl; Baby.java and Cfg.java are the only files that differ from z3x). When hostile and not rescuing, a baby with 12000+ real bytecodes left runs GrabMicro.act. It scores staying and each one-step tile with each facing by a grab there, a bite (more when it ends the victim's health edge or kills) and minus 25 for each enemy that could step next to it into its blind spot (anywhere next to it when that enemy is healthier). It takes the best option when that beats standing by 10, else it marks the clearly worse steps as avoided. A turn the micro leaves under BC_BAIL (3500) ends there.
